From 4fb1761cd8fa5af6af081faa49797422c809d5a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heresy <heresy@local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:48:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1009/1178] Player plays on down the list; card prompt and
 lyrics fold; style warnings

HERESY 1009.
- Player: previous and next take buttons, and "Play on" (on by default, kept
  per browser): when a take ends, the next one down the list starts, into the
  history. A take card that shows the playing take follows it.
- Take card: Prompt and Lyrics fold on a click on their heading and start
  folded; folded, the heading shows the size and the first line.
- The style counter flags what the 110 official example styles never hold:
  more than 999 characters, arrows, dynamics marks, three or more "Label:"
  fields; and note lines in (brackets) inside the lyrics, which the official
  skill keeps out ("Keep implementation notes out of lyrics").
- Style and lyrics help rewritten on those numbers; the old text counted a
  4,096 score and a 9,000 song and invited 40,000 characters of style.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
